<ServicePage {...content} schema={[repairSchema]}>
  <ServiceSection heading={"Expert Repairs You Can Trust"} image="/photos/photo-eye-replacement.webp" imageAlt="Garage door sensor repair and replacement">
    <p> From broken springs and frayed cables to bent tracks and worn rollers, we've seen (and fixed) it all. Our repairs restore your door's safety, reliability, and smooth operation—without the runaround or upselling. </p>
    <p> We diagnose the root cause, explain what's wrong in plain English, and fix it right the first time. Every repair includes full system testing and balancing before we leave. </p>
  </ServiceSection>

  <ServiceSection heading={"Common Garage Door Problems We Fix"} tone="sand">
    <ul><li><strong>Door won't open or close</strong> — stuck halfway, won't respond to remote, or opens but won't close</li><li><strong>Off-track or crooked door</strong> — door hanging at an angle, jammed, or completely off the tracks</li><li><strong>Loud noises</strong> — grinding, squealing, banging, or rattling sounds during operation</li><li><strong>Broken or frayed cables</strong> — visible cable damage, coiled up, or hanging loose</li><li><strong>Worn rollers or hinges</strong> — door moves rough, jerks during operation, or makes grinding noise</li><li><strong>Bent or damaged tracks</strong> — door sticks in spots, won't close fully, or jumps off track</li><li><strong>Door closes too fast or slams</strong> — sign of broken spring (dangerous—don't use it)</li><li><strong>Sensor issues</strong> — door reverses immediately, won't close at all, or sensor lights blinking</li><li><strong>Damaged panels</strong> — dented, cracked, or broken door sections affecting appearance or function</li></ul>
    <p><strong>Not sure what's wrong?</strong> From mystery squeaks to complete breakdowns, our technicians arrive to fix any issue. <a href="/contact">Book Your Repair</a> now. </p>
  </ServiceSection>

  <ServiceSection heading={"Why Act Quickly on Garage Door Repairs"}>
    <p> We get it—garage door repairs aren't fun, and it's tempting to put them off. But ignoring problems leads to bigger (and more expensive) issues down the road: </p>
    <ul><li><strong>Safety risk:</strong> A malfunctioning door can fall unexpectedly, causing injury or property damage</li><li><strong>Worse damage:</strong> Small problems (worn rollers, loose hardware) cause bigger failures (bent tracks, broken springs)</li><li><strong>Higher repair costs:</strong> Delaying a $150 roller replacement can lead to a $400 track repair</li><li><strong>Opener damage:</strong> Operating a door with broken parts strains your opener motor, shortening its lifespan</li><li><strong>Security risk:</strong> A door that won't close leaves your home and belongings vulnerable</li></ul>
    <p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> If your door is acting up, get it checked. Early repairs are faster, cheaper, and safer. </p>
    <p><a href="/homeowner-tools/easy-estimate#estimate-form" class="btn btn--primary">Get Instant Repair Estimate</a></p>
  </ServiceSection>

